Luhn: 
The code starts with initializing a string of garbage numbers
Asks for 16 digit number
First loops to check if it is 16 digits long
Then loops to check if all of them are digits
After it checks all of that, it then goes into a loop to starting to add the digits together from the last digit up to the first.
Every second digit is doubled per the rules of the Luhn and this is done with a true or false statement switching back and forth every iteration.
When it is true it will double the digit and if it is greater than 9 it will subtract it by 9 until it is a single digit, then adds to the sum.
After it gets through all elements it goes to a if statement t ocheck if it is divisble by 10. This is done with finding the remainder to be 0.
It then prints out whether or not it is a valid card.
